# Clipboard Viewer: the keys of arch311-ref/scn/clipbrd-wmf.scn (tools/ref311/scenario.py w16)
# Opens SYSTEM\CBWMF.CLP (an anisotropic picture: rectangle, ellipse, line, text), stretched to the
# window; the Display menu; saves WMF.CLP. The 48 pixels allowed are single pixels on the ellipse's
# outline, where libw16's Ellipse differs from 3.1's GDI scan conversion (not the viewer's doing).
# compare: clipbrd-wmf/03.png 01.png ignore 320 240 333 261 max 48
# compare: clipbrd-wmf/04.png 02.png ignore 320 240 333 261 max 48
# compare: clipbrd-wmf/06.png 03.png ignore 320 240 333 261 max 48
# file: files/wmf.clp run-clipbrd-wmf/WINDOWS/WMF.CLP apps/clipbrd/tests/clpcmp.py
# regress: sh apps/clipbrd/tests/run.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
sleep 400
key alt
key f
key o
key s
key y
key s
key t
key e
key m
key backslash
key c
key b
key w
key m
key f
key period
key c
key l
key p
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
key alt
key d
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
key esc
key esc
key alt
key f
key a
key w
key m
key f
key period
key c
key l
key p
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
quit
